## Summary of the Change

The core fix, per the commit message, is to update the re-lexing logic to `"avoid consuming the trailing whitespace and move the lexer explicitly to the last newline character"`. Rather than tracking a separate `new_position` alongside a boolean `has_newline` flag, the code now records the exact `newline_position` in an `Option`, so the cursor is repositioned precisely at the newline instead of anywhere within trailing whitespace.

The bug (issue #11929) only appeared when a comment had trailing whitespace, since otherwise the lexer would simply skip over the whitespace. The overlapping token ranges caused a panic. The `.py` resource file adds a test case reproducing this with an f-string followed by a comment with trailing spaces, and the snapshot file was updated accordingly.

